divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:15:04-07:00","id":974547,"title":"","content":"Skimming through the early access version, and this is looking quite good.<br /> <br /> What I got from the Theoi document, though: Hestia is bestia? (\u00baw\u00ba)<br /> (More seriously, I very much like the write-ups of the gods and the greek Terra Incognita.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:17:17-07:00","id":974549,"title":"","content":"Double funded in an hour and fifteen minutes. Wow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:24:27-07:00","id":974553,"title":"","content":"It's going to take me a second to wrap my head around how Enhancements and Complications work, but overall I'm in love. Do you think there's any chance of a character creation spoiler?<br /> <br /> And that Theoi section us great, but it just makes me hungry for the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:25:00-07:00","id":974554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974549#post974549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double funded in an hour and fifteen minutes. Wow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two hours fifteen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:38:50-07:00","id":974560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974547#post974547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skimming through the early access version, and this is looking quite good.<br /> <br /> What I got from the Theoi document, though: Hestia is bestia? (\u00baw\u00ba)<br /> (More seriously, I very much like the write-ups of the gods and the greek Terra Incognita.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, she's the only Theoi not known for causing plagues and disasters due to the Celestial Idealistic Game of Thrones. She's Bestia by default, along with Persephone.<br /> <br /> Can I say I actually respect Zeus now, too? He's a consummate politician <i>in the process </i>of being an okay patriarch-a child who likes you isn't likely to invoke that patricide Fate any time soon...<br /> <br /> Also, Hydras decapitating their pups to allow safe head growth. That, right there, just perfect worldbuilding. Perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:43:20-07:00","id":974562,"title":"","content":"Only real gripe I see so far is there is too much &quot;if the player accepts&quot; being mentioned. Seems like it makes the ST at the mercy of his players more so than usual. Botch seems to be only given if the ST wants it to happen and the player agrees. Maybe it's just my group but my player's don't like to lose at all but they accept it because it happens. I think I'll still be using the idea that if u get zero successes and one of those is a nat 1 then you botch. And I'll likely give complications or consolations if its story fitting rather than player choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:46:25-07:00","id":974563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974562#post974562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only real gripe I see so far is there is too much &quot;if the player accepts&quot; being mentioned. Seems like it makes the ST at the mercy of his players more so than usual. Botch seems to be only given if the ST wants it to happen and the player agrees. Maybe it's just my group but my player's don't like to lose at all but they accept it because it happens. I think I'll still be using the idea that if u get zero successes and one of those is a nat 1 then you botch. And I'll likely give complications or consolations if its story fitting rather than player choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Problem-if that happens, things get really boring real quick. Just roll to succeed-fail. Roll to succeed-fail. Etcetera.<br /> <br /> And the ST does get Tension rules to pay the players back. And Complications...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:52:07-07:00","id":974565,"title":"","content":"Succeed or fail has worked in systems for years. I mean, I love how the system tries to alliviate dead ends but I think most experienced story writing STs already do that. I just really dislike the idea that a botch is a back and forth discussion rather than a shocking moment you resolve and keep going with the aftermath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:54:22-07:00","id":974566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974562#post974562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only real gripe I see so far is there is too much &amp;quot;if the player accepts&amp;quot; being mentioned. Seems like it makes the ST at the mercy of his players more so than usual. Botch seems to be only given if the ST wants it to happen and the player agrees. Maybe it's just my group but my player's don't like to lose at all but they accept it because it happens. I think I'll still be using the idea that if u get zero successes and one of those is a nat 1 then you botch. And I'll likely give complications or consolations if its story fitting rather than player choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're about a decade late to the current narrative game school of design. Storypath has FATE and PbtA fingerprints all over it, and with good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:09:23-07:00","id":974580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974565#post974565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Succeed or fail has worked in systems for years. I mean, I love how the system tries to alliviate dead ends but I think most experienced story writing STs already do that. I just really dislike the idea that a botch is a back and forth discussion rather than a shocking moment you resolve and keep going with the aftermath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you can change that back and forth thing to a simpler Succeed or Fail without too much harm to the Storypath System. It is actually designed to let you engage the more collaborative storytelling aspects as they work for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:10:40-07:00","id":974582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974566#post974566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're about a decade late to the current narrative game school of design. Storypath has FATE and PbtA fingerprints all over it, and with good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like my view is wrong. (Not sure if thats the intent) Clearly I'm in the minority here or have a dated way of thinking so if that's the case is there anyone here willing to give me examples as to why it works better and how I should argue that same case to players who are unfamilier with it? I'm fine with being told im wrong, provided the other person can tell me why. I'm also the type of person to want to learn/adapt if I got a bad perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:17:36-07:00","id":974587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974582#post974582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that like my view is wrong. (Not sure if thats the intent) Clearly I'm in the minority here or have a dated way of thinking so if that's the case is there anyone here willing to give me examples as to why it works better and how I should argue that same case to players who are unfamilier with it? I'm fine with being told im wrong, provided the other person can tell me why. I'm also the type of person to want to learn/adapt if I got a bad perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least for me, a game where the Game Master/Storyteller/Storyguide/Keeper of Arcane Secrets/whatever is soundly in charge of the narrative with the player characters are pretty much exclusively a reactionary role is boring to me. Many games in recent years (especially among the indie scene) have been working to break down the wall between GM and players in terms of wider control over the narrative (beyond just deciding what your own character can do), since tabletop roleplaying is already a collaborative exercise. <br /> <br /> Having the dice fail isn't interactive in the least. Having the dice fail you and getting to decide if you want to succeed at a cost anyway, have something else happen, or let things go catastrophically wrong is by contrast much more engaging and fun, and lets players have more of a hand in the story. &quot;Why would I ever want to botch?&quot; is very much an old-school &quot;I want to win the game&quot; mentality, whereas taking the botch in the name of drama (and Momentum to spend on a later, more critical roll) is better for the story.<br /> <br /> Sorry to come off a little harsh. I'm used to lots and lots of hardcore grognards losing their minds whenever any sort of story-focused indie game comes up and it makes me defensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:35:01-07:00","id":974599,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't Zeus (or at least the Jupiter mantle) have Beasts (Eagle) as a purview? They're pretty central to his image and his worship.<br /> <br /> It is not a coincidence that it became a symbol of Rome and its legions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:40:11-07:00","id":974600,"title":"","content":"I'm all for differing opinions as long as they know they are opinions. Point remains is some players out there still prefer to react rather than collab a story. My players are the type that loath playing a ST role and want to know how their character would react in a given situation. Only one of my players actually enjoys being a dungeon master/story teller for his own games. They want to know what happened, not work with me on what happened. Generally speaking I think there is only 1 player out of the 5 who tries to work with me on how events unfold after the dice is rolled. I think if I gave them a choice atleast one of them would respond &quot;Which one is better?&quot; which is clearly against the idea of the rules as written. I guess my players want to feel like they are somewhat at the mercy of the events in game. Sort of gives it a stronger grittier horror vibe which I tend to run my games with.<br /> <br /> I fully see why a interactive story system would be great and I do see the benefits of trying to teach my group to be more compatible with a system like this but it seems like quite a big undertaking and something that may turn them off of scion 2nd edition as likely as it would spur them to change. And quite honestly, I love Scion overall way too much to want to risk that. I really do like most of what I'm reading so far though.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks for the post Rich. Good to know that there wouldn't be too many issues with that if I modify to be a bit more old school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-22-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:44:09-07:00","id":974605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974600#post974600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my players want to feel like they are somewhat at the mercy of the events in game. Sort of gives it a stronger grittier horror vibe which I tend to run my games with.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Scion isn't gritty or horror, it's urban fantasy/adventure on the brink of pulp or outright superhero. <br /> <br /> It's clear we don't agree here, so I won't bother the thread with it more. Sorry you don't like the new rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:51:34-07:00","id":974608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974605#post974605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Scion isn't gritty or horror, it's urban fantasy/adventure on the brink of pulp or outright superhero.<br /> <br /> It's clear we don't agree here, so I won't bother the thread with it more. Sorry you don't like the new rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>You certainly are a all or nothing sort of guy, huh? I DO like the new rules and CAN see the value in them. I just think they are clearly a better fit for a group of players who enjoy a more collaborative approach to tabletop than old school.<br /> <br /> Also, Scion isn't gritty or horror? I assure you that it can be. You haven't heard of brutal events that happen to heroes in mythology? I mean, I know most the stories are of the people who made it through all covered in gore and victory but that isnt the only side of mythology. My players want to be challenged with a good likelyhood that dangerous encounters could result in one of the characters taking a dirt nap afterwards. That being the case doesn't change or detract from their interest in playing as children of gods and delving deep into mythology though.<br /> <br /> I know a few of my players who are looking forward to playing as mortals in a horror themed campaign in The World. What's the different between a psycho chasing you around with an axe or a saytr chasing you around with an axe? Pretty sure its just the horns and hooves.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day its all just different strokes for different folks. And I am going to play/run the hell out of scion 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hell, if they add more $400 dollar reward tiers you may see a fat IT nerd scion (me) who gets his visitation after clicking on a odd file on his desktop called Thor.exe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-22-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:52:18-07:00","id":974609,"title":"","content":"So guess on which pantheon is next Yatazas or Nemotedemos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:55:13-07:00","id":974610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974608#post974608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You certainly are a all or nothing sort of guy, huh? I DO like the new rules and CAN see the value in them. I just think they are clearly a better fit for a group of players who enjoy a more collaborative approach to tabletop than old school.<br /> <br /> Also, Scion isn't gritty or horror? I assure you that it can be. You haven't heard of brutal events that happen to heroes in mythology? I mean, I know most the stories are of the people who made it through all covered in gore and victory but that isnt the only side of mythology. My players want to be challenged with a good likelyhood that dangerous encounters could result in one of the characters taking a dirt nap afterwards. That being the case doesn't change or detract from their interest in playing as children of gods and delving deep into mythology though.<br /> <br /> I know a few of my players who are looking forward to a more modern horror themed campaign in The World. What's the different between a psycho chasing you around with an axe or a saytr chasing you around with an axe? Pretty sure its just the horns and hooves.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day its all just different strokes for different folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a guy, and the game itself isn't horror even if some mythology is. Scion is pretty explicitly a counter to the folks who like the World of Darkness as urban fantasy but loathe the horror in it. You play competent people with superheroic abilities; fighting scary monsters does not horror make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:58:01-07:00","id":974612,"title":"","content":"Well, hopefully both our groups have fun with the game. That's all that really matters in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:58:04-07:00","id":974613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974609#post974609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So guess on which pantheon is next Yatazas or Nemotedemos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yazatas, I think has been said here before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:02:40-07:00","id":974619,"title":"","content":"Oh I ment which one is the next stretch goal but that makes sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:04:27-07:00","id":974622,"title":"","content":"I'll admit to being a little bummed that Hecate isn't in the Theoi section. I get that wordcount is hell and it's easy to add new gods, but I love her so much. Seeing who does and doesn't make the cut for the Netjer will be agony.<br /> <br /> I hope we can see some more spoilers soon; I've been waiting to hear about Geneses for months now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:13:57-07:00","id":974629,"title":"","content":"Gallic Pantheon's next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Sola