_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T20:57:40-07:00","id":974854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974853#post974853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for one Armorican village \u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Stupid house rules. Alchemy is supposed to be the Shen's PSP.<br /> <br /> Also, new stretch goals: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At $120,000, we'll expand the Scion Companion PDF with a section providing a translation guide from Scion 1e to Scion 2nd Edition rules and setting.<br /> At $135,000, we will start the Scion 2nd Edition Fiction Anthology PDF/ePub with the first three stories. Backers who pledge for any reward tier including PDFs of Scion: Origin andScion: Hero will receive this PDF/ePub. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T21:08:35-07:00","id":974860,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why you need a Translation Guide when just rebuilding your characters seem easier, but far be it from me to complain about more content. Fiction anthologies have never scratched any itches for me, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Will we see any more Pantheons beyond the Yazata, or are those firmly in the realm of later books? I'm dying for more mechanical stuff we can actually use, rather than fiction or collectible goodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T00:40:56-07:00","id":974926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974599#post974599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Zeus (or at least the Jupiter mantle) have Beasts (Eagle) as a purview? They're pretty central to his image and his worship.<br /> <br /> It is not a coincidence that it became a symbol of Rome and its legions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't seak for the Devs, but so many gods are associated with specific animals that I think they'll be a bit more stingy with who does and doesn't get the Beasts Purview. If you look at the Theoi I think only Artemis gets it, which makes sense as a goddess of the hunt. But Athena doesn't get Beasts (Owl), despite the owl being one of her most recognizable symbols (I mean it's still on some Greek euro coins to this day!).<br /> <br /> So I think we'll only see gods with the Beast purview when animals are really part of their nature, rather than just a symbol associated with them. The eagle is a symbol of Zeus =/= Zeus is a god of eagles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T00:46:50-07:00","id":974928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974926#post974926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can't seak for the Devs, but so many gods are associated with specific animals that I think they'll be a bit more stingy with who does and doesn't get the Beasts Purview. If you look at the Theoi I think only Artemis gets it, which makes sense as a goddess of the hunt. But Athena doesn't get Beasts (Owl), despite the owl being one of her most recognizable symbols (I mean it's still on some Greek euro coins to this day!).<br /> <br /> So I think we'll only see gods with the Beast purview when animals are really part of their nature, rather than just a symbol associated with them. The eagle is a symbol of Zeus =/= Zeus is a god of eagles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, they can't include all possible purviews one could argue for, for each god. However, I would note that Athena <i>does</i> have Beasts (Owl).<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Poseidon gets Beasts (Horse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","user":"GSD","date":". 09-23-2016, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T00:59:45-07:00","id":974931,"title":"","content":"I've never used Kickstarter before, and it's not that I distrust Onyx Path or anything, but...<br /> <br /> I added the +$25 and it didn't mention anything about the 1st Edition PDFS when it listed the rewards I would get. I'm mildly worried. Did I do something wrong, or is it supposed to be like that?<br /> <br /> If it helps, I had to play +$55 fo shipping as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T01:38:15-07:00","id":974937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974931#post974931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never used Kickstarter before, and it's not that I distrust Onyx Path or anything, but...<br /> <br /> I added the +$25 and it didn't mention anything about the 1st Edition PDFS when it listed the rewards I would get. I'm mildly worried. Did I do something wrong, or is it supposed to be like that?<br /> <br /> If it helps, I had to play +$55 fo shipping as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to select the reward tier in the right-hand sidebar that you want to get.<br /> <br /> Then you add addons by directly modifying your pledge. At some point (possibly backerkit? I don't know what OPP uses for this) you'll be asked to list what your addons are based on your additional pledge. It won't show up until then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:01:21-07:00","id":974941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974928#post974928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, sure, they can't include all possible purviews one could argue for, for each god. However, I would note that Athena <i>does</i> have Beasts (Owl).<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Poseidon gets Beasts (Horse).</div> </div> </div> </div>I pushed back on having the whole Greek pantheon getting their sacred animals as Beasts subdomains\u2014Hera doesn't really go around using peacock powers in the myth. Athena and Poseidon have mythic reasons for having the Beasts Purview.<br /> <br /> If you want to see a pantheon where everyone has Beasts, you'll have to look to the Netjer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:51:56-07:00","id":974960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974937#post974937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need to select the reward tier in the right-hand sidebar that you want to get.<br /> <br /> Then you add addons by directly modifying your pledge. At some point (possibly backerkit? I don't know what OPP uses for this) you'll be asked to list what your addons are based on your additional pledge. It won't show up until then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I selected my pledge and put the extra money in the pledge. I guess now I just... wait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T03:09:48-07:00","id":974966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974960#post974960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I selected my pledge and put the extra money in the pledge. I guess now I just... wait?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just wait. You won't be asked until after the kickstarter is finished, at least that's how it's worked in other kickstarters I've participated in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T03:29:16-07:00","id":974969,"title":"","content":"Okay, little help here. I do not quite get damage calculation.<br /> You get damaged for three stress and note it in thethree box, then you take 1 stress. This does mean, than you must mark the 4th box, or take injury, if you do not want to mark another box right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T04:42:01-07:00","id":974991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974969#post974969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, little help here. I do not quite get damage calculation.<br /> You get damaged for three stress and note it in thethree box, then you take 1 stress. This does mean, than you must mark the 4th box, or take injury, if you do not want to mark another box right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like you mark the 1st box, or take an injury if you don't want to mark another box. And you are only taken out when all of your boxes are full. But you can take an endless amount of injury complications. That's probably not working as intended, but it doesn't say otherwise. It's really confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T04:43:12-07:00","id":974992,"title":"","content":"I hope the dice are in the next set of stretch goals!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:10:27-07:00","id":974999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974991#post974991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like you mark the 1st box, or take an injury if you don't want to mark another box. And you are only taken out when all of your boxes are full. But you can take an endless amount of injury complications. That's probably not working as intended, but it doesn't say otherwise. It's really confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda hope that is not the case, because it means you have to hit(hit, not attack many times per bigger fight) This is villain 6 hits+2 amazon 4 hits each and enough mooks to make it cinematic. It is minimum of 14 hits. Assuming 50% average hit and 5 players it s over 5 rounds of a rather dull combat encounter. it swells hard with more oponents, which makes combat more interesting That is a lot of turns and rolls and I would not consider this really big figh, just decently sized one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:22:08-07:00","id":975004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974999#post974999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda hope that is not the case, because it means you have to hit(hit, not attack many times per bigger fight) This is villain 6 hits+2 amazon 4 hits each and enough mooks to make it cinematic. It is minimum of 14 hits. Assuming 50% average hit and 5 players it s over 5 rounds of a rather dull combat encounter. it swells hard with more oponents, which makes combat more interesting That is a lot of turns and rolls and I would not consider this really big figh, just decently sized one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see fights taking several hours. Even a Hydra has 10 stress, so I'm really wondering about the demigod and god level enemies. Maybe demigods and gods will have a way to damage multiple stress boxes at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:46:32-07:00","id":975010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975004#post975004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see fights taking several hours. Even a Hydra has 10 stress, so I'm really wondering about the demigod and god level enemies. Maybe demigods and gods will have a way to damage multiple stress boxes at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think the combat rules are in rough draft form without a whole lot of polish. I figure Neall will clarify a bit when he can or already knows they improved them in a newer version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:47:11-07:00","id":975011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975004#post975004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see fights taking several hours. Even a Hydra has 10 stress, so I'm really wondering about the demigod and god level enemies. Maybe demigods and gods will have a way to damage multiple stress boxes at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>dont forget though that at these lvls then scale comes into play so its possible they dont have much more stress boxes in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:50:39-07:00","id":975013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975011#post975011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">dont forget though that at these lvls then scale comes into play so its possible they dont have much more stress boxes in reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scale is relative. Which means you won't be getting bonuses for scale unless your scale is higher than that of the hydra. If its being used as a big scarey boss then most likely it is getting scale bonuses on you instead.<br /> <br /> EDIT: However, I do not see any mention of scale on any of the sample antagonists so I honestly have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-23-2016, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:01:32-07:00","id":975016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975013#post975013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scale is relative. Which means you won't be getting bonuses for scale unless your scale is higher than that of the hydra. If its being used as a big scarey boss then most likely it is getting scale bonuses on you instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly or if you are a demigod you are of a speicif scale (same for god) while the hydra is also at its own scale. Thus there is POSSIBLYno need for more stress boxes. But in essence only one who can answer this is a dev.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:45:59-07:00","id":975029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974941#post974941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pushed back on having the whole Greek pantheon getting their sacred animals as Beasts subdomains\u2014Hera doesn't really go around using peacock powers in the myth. Athena and Poseidon have mythic reasons for having the Beasts Purview.<br /> <br /> If you want to see a pantheon where everyone has Beasts, you'll have to look to the Netjer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! Thanks for the input!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:17:31-07:00","id":975035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974991#post974991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like you mark the 1st box, or take an injury if you don't want to mark another box. And you are only taken out when all of your boxes are full. But you can take an endless amount of injury complications. That's probably not working as intended, but it doesn't say otherwise. It's really confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't come in, but you can only take -1, -1, -2, -2, -4 Injury Complications before you can't take any more. Mooks don't have any ICs, only stress; some enemies can take more ICs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:18:05-07:00","id":975037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975013#post975013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: However, I do not see any mention of scale on any of the sample antagonists so I honestly have no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those got weirdly dropped. We have suggested Scale for the antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:19:06-07:00","id":975038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974860#post974860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why you need a Translation Guide when just rebuilding your characters seem easier, but far be it from me to complain about more content.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll be a stealth &quot;this is how to build a character&quot; advice guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:39:28-07:00","id":975043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975035#post975035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't come in, but you can only take -1, -1, -2, -2, -4 Injury Complications before you can't take any more. Mooks don't have any ICs, only stress; some enemies can take more ICs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you possibly clarify a little about how damage is tracked? Several of us seem to be very confused by it. My main question is what happens if u take 1 point of stress damage but already have all your -1 complication slots full as well as your 1st stress damage box filled in your vitality track?<br /> <br /> I'm totally fine with the system overall if a character ALWAYS fills a minimum of 1 box every successfully damaging hit weather that be a complication or a vitality box. Basically any remaining stress that can't be placed in your remaining boxes instead fills the next highest possible. At least that way you wont sit there with all your boxes except your last vitality one completely full just waiting for the enemy to hit you hard enough to mark that last box while shrugging off everything else. I mean, you already can't die by something on a lower scale than you so making it super difficult for one of the same or one scale higher to deliver a take out blow in general seems weird.<br /> <br /> We appreciate any insight you can give to alleviate confusion or give us some perspective on why it was designed this way specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-23-2016, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:59:47-07:00","id":975054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975043#post975043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you possibly clarify a little about how damage is tracked? Several of us seem to be very confused by it. My main question is what happens if u take 1 point of stress damage but already have all your -1 complication slots full as well as your 1st stress damage box filled in your vitality track?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of folks seem confused, so yeah, we need to rewrite it. The answer is that you take another point of Vitality stress damage - it marks off the next available tick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:21:03-07:00","id":975059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975054#post975054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of folks seem confused, so yeah, we need to rewrite it. The answer is that you take another point of Vitality stress damage - it marks off the next available tick.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if in this case the next vitality slot would be their 3rd one but they have a -2 complication slot available would they then be able to take a -2 complication instead for that 1 stress damage? If so, this system certainly works for me. Gives a sort of increasing value to each point of stamina someone decides to invest in. Means 1 stamina characters are nearly always going to get injured every time they get into a scrap and take a hit.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the response, Neall. That's why we like you being in charge of this thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-23-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T09:06:17-07:00","id":975085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975054#post975054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of folks seem confused, so yeah, we need to rewrite it. The answer is that you take another point of Vitality stress damage - it marks off the next available tick.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about extreme damage? What if someone hits you for like 10 successes over threshold? Since vitality is not ablative, do you just mark off your highest vitality and the rest vanishes into the ether?<br /> <br /> How about 3 damage? What if you want to give yourself an injury complication of -3, but there are no -3 injury complication slots?<br /> <br /> How about backwards damage? If you have low defense, the bad guys might have a hard time getting exactly 1 threshold success. Do they keep hitting you until they do poorly enough to score 1 success, or can damage go backwards on the track?<br /> <br /> Will there be features that do more than one stress level of damage at a time to speed up combat?<br /> <br /> I'm really loving a lot of stuff in the Kickstarter, but combat is like a jigsaw puzzle right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T11:06:18-07:00","id":975131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974941#post974941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pushed back on having the whole Greek pantheon getting their sacred animals as Beasts subdomains\u2014Hera doesn't really go around using peacock powers in the myth. Athena and Poseidon have mythic reasons for having the Beasts Purview.<br /> <br /> If you want to see a pantheon where everyone has Beasts, you'll have to look to the Netjer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, can know which god Ra was merged with anyone in this edition of the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-23-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T11:33:38-07:00","id":975141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975131#post975131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, can know which god Ra was merged with anyone in this edition of the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess at the Netjer, I would go Ra, Heru, Sutek, Hathor, Aset, Azar, Bast, Sobek, and then probably Ptah and Khnum. If space wasn't a factor, I'd split Sekhmet from Bast and toss in some more niche ones like Nekhbet, Maahes, and Wepawet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T11:37:43-07:00","id":975144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975141#post975141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I had to guess at the Netjer, I would go Ra, Heru, Sutek, Hathor, Aset, Azar, Bast, Sobek, and then probably Ptah and Khnum. If space wasn't a factor, I'd split Sekhmet from Bast and toss in some more niche ones like Nekhbet, Maahes, and Wepawet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think Neall's tagged Hathor as a Mantle of Aset.<br /> <br /> And no Djehuti?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T11:46:48-07:00","id":975146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975144#post975144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think Neall's tagged Hathor as a Mantle of Aset.<br /> <br /> And no Djehuti?</div> </div> </div> </div>...I have shamed myself.<br /> <br /> I also forgot to mention Shezmu in my niche god listing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:06:57-07:00","id":975155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=974941#post974941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pushed back on having the whole Greek pantheon getting their sacred animals as Beasts subdomains\u2014Hera doesn't really go around using peacock powers in the myth. Athena and Poseidon have mythic reasons for having the Beasts Purview.<br /> <br /> If you want to see a pantheon where everyone has Beasts, you'll have to look to the Netjer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I was expecting that to a degree, but I guess I was considering eagles to be closer to Poseidon than Hera, in terms of animal relevance.<br /> <br /> It ultimately isn't a big deal. But it is nice to know it is, in fact, intentional.<br /> <br /> Edit: Is it possible for different aliases, like Zeus vs Jupiter, or Mars vs Ares, to have (slightly) different purviews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","user":"GSD","date":". 09-23-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:58:23-07:00","id":975243,"title":"","content":"Wow, I had no ideas Kieron Gillen wrote comics! I used to devour his reviews and articles in PC Gamer UK years ago, really excited about this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:31:20-07:00","id":975253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975144#post975144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think Neall's tagged Hathor as a Mantle of Aset</div> </div> </div> </div> That is... Weird to me. They were pretty distinctly worshipped from each other. There's the motherhood overlap, but you see that a lot with goddesses.<br /> <br /> Aset definitely doesn't turn into Sekhmet too and need to get drunk on beer to turn back.<br /> <br /> And then if you're equating Sekhmet with Bast too, you're pretty much shoving all the major goddesses into one figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T19:35:32-07:00","id":975338,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Companion caps out at the three Pantheons Neall's mentioned for it (2 of which we've already unlocked, the third being the Yazata), or if there's room for some others if the kickstarter is successful enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T20:06:44-07:00","id":975349,"title":"","content":"Is there any reason that the stretch goals are so much more spread out then previous Kickstarters? Like, BtP had stretch goals every few thousand dollars, whereas Scion is almost always 15,000 dollars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T20:13:55-07:00","id":975351,"title":"","content":"Hit 120k. Not bad for a second day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T20:17:40-07:00","id":975352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975338#post975338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Companion caps out at the three Pantheons Neall's mentioned for it (2 of which we've already unlocked, the third being the Yazata), or if there's room for some others if the kickstarter is successful enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that Demigod and God each have five Pantheons in them plus stretch goals for their Kickstarter(s) and then try to imagine which Pantheons have both enough material in them to write about and writers knowledgeable enough in them to write those sections. Pantheons are definitely the sexiest add-ons, but also some of the hardest.<br /> <br /> That said, gimme more Pantheons!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:54:02-07:00","id":975396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975349#post975349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reason that the stretch goals are so much more spread out then previous Kickstarters? Like, BtP had stretch goals every few thousand dollars, whereas Scion is almost always 15,000 dollars</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing because most of them are fairly chunky - Jumpstart, translation guide, pantheons, three anthology stories...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:58:20-07:00","id":975399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975253#post975253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is... Weird to me. They were pretty distinctly worshipped from each other. There's the motherhood overlap, but you see that a lot with goddesses.<br /> <br /> Aset definitely doesn't turn into Sekhmet too and need to get drunk on beer to turn back.<br /> <br /> And then if you're equating Sekhmet with Bast too, you're pretty much shoving all the major goddesses into one figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>As best I can tell, the only equations Neall's offered are Hathor - Aset and Sekhmet - Bast. He's <i>not</i> made the Hathor - Sekhmet equation that would merge them all into one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T00:12:57-07:00","id":975406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975349#post975349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reason that the stretch goals are so much more spread out then previous Kickstarters? Like, BtP had stretch goals every few thousand dollars, whereas Scion is almost always 15,000 dollars</div> </div> </div> </div>marin has already said this, but I'd say it's because they are reasonably big additions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T00:16:38-07:00","id":975407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975399#post975399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As best I can tell, the only equations Neall's offered are Hathor - Aset and Sekhmet - Bast. He's <i>not</i> made the Hathor - Sekhmet equation that would merge them all into one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Hathor merger is pretty inexplicable to me, as Aset is pretty profoundly the magic goddess first and foremost to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:09:57-07:00","id":975500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975399#post975399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As best I can tell, the only equations Neall's offered are Hathor - Aset and Sekhmet - Bast. He's <i>not</i> made the Hathor - Sekhmet equation that would merge them all into one.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the one with the actual myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:45:19-07:00","id":975511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/952910-kickstarter-soon?p=975500#post975500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's the one with the actual myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall first brought up merging Bast and Sekhmet here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We made the somewhat controversial decision to merge Bast and Sekhmet, with Bastet being a later mantle/personality. The Egyptian pantheon, not unlike the Greco-Roman pantheon, presents difficulties where you can point to a god early in their religion's timeline and go &quot;these are clearly the same god&quot; but a couple of hundred new cities and a few years and they've <i>never</i> been the same god, how could you think that? Is Ptah actually Sokar or Tetenen, and is he married to Bast or Sehkmet or both? Thankfully, a lot of this is politics, and allows us to do interesting things like talk about how these singular beings change over time and use mantles to keep cognitive dissonance to a minimum. </div> </div> </div>I asked about Sekhmet being Hathor, or Hathor being her own independent goddess, to which he answered:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hathor got merged with Isis.<br /> <br /> This whole discussion has caused a new sidebar to appear in the text:<br /> <br /> &quot;Divinity is not a static thing, even outside the world of <b>Scion</b>. Take the Goddess Sekhmet, for example: in the Upper Kingdom, she was the lioness goddess of war, yet there was a parallel deity with many (though not all) of the same attributes, called Bast, in the Lower Kingdom. Many parallel deities were much the same, and merged seamlessly when the Kingdoms unified, but Sekhmet stayed Sekhmet and Bast became Bastet, known more as a protector deity.<br /> Many gods across many pantheons change, alter, split apart from other gods and merge with others. Accuracy in myth is a shifting line over time, weaving through thousands of years of politics, art, and religion. <b>Scion</b>, however, must consider these beings to be largely singular who change over time. Judgment calls must be made: we posit that Sekhmet/Bastet began wild and untamed, but her love of beer has mellowed her into a fierce protector, a separate mantle known as Bast. If you or your group disagree, or want to use them as twin sister Scions of Ra who went two separate ways later in life, that\u2019s perfectly fine - just create new Callings and assign Purviews.&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:42:40-07:00","id":975589,"title":"","content":"Oh my goodness, we have to hit 150,000, CULTS have to be in the game and more importantly FAR RANGING PURVIEWS!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:39:41-07:00","id":975624,"title":"","content":"Yeah, cults looks like a good stretch goal for the companion book.<br /> <br /> Would like to see another big stretch goal after this one, something like a book completely focused on giving more details on pantheons that we already have or one about antagonists inspired by different myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12264-isengrim","name":"Isengrim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:45:51-07:00","id":975626,"title":"","content":"That'd be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T12:04:56-07:00","id":975631,"title":"","content":"I like Cults, but I'm worried that we won't get the Yatza at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"M